<title>JAPAN: Nippon Oil 26,000 bpd topper to restart as planned.</title>
<headline>Nippon Oil 26,000 bpd topper to restart as planned.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Oil Co Ltd said on Friday that a 26,000 barrel-per-day (bpd) crude distillation unit at its Niigata plant in northern Japan will resume operations on Saturday as originally scheduled.</p>
<p>The topper has been closed since August 29 for a routine turnaround, a refinery spokesman said.</p>
</text>
